  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "In \\(\\triangle ABC\\) and \\(\\triangle DEF\\), \\(AB=DE\\) and \\(AC=DF\\). Which additional condition allows the two triangles to be proved congruent by SAS?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\angle A=\\angle D\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\angle B=\\angle E\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\angle C=\\angle F\\)",
    "D": "\\(BC=EF\\)"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The included angle between \\(AB\\) and \\(AC\\) is \\(\\angle A\\), and the included angle between \\(DE\\) and \\(DF\\) is \\(\\angle D\\), so \\(\\angle A=\\angle D\\) is required. The condition \\(BC=EF\\) corresponds to SSS.",
